cff-version: 1.2.0
title: web-attack-atlas
message: If you use this atlas in research or a report, cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gounder
    given-names: Harsh
    alias: harshgounder
repository-code: https://github.com/harshgounder/web-attack-atlas
url: https://github.com/harshgounder/web-attack-atlas
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
abstract: >
  A pattern atlas for web platform attacks organised by state mutation rather than vulnerability class.
  150 patterns across three write domains, each answering five questions (what state changes, as whom,
  does it persist, how do you know, what stops it) and each carrying a counter with its own precondition
  and cost. Built on 16 attack primitives, with a machine readable decision tree per domain.
keywords:
  - application security
  - web security
  - attack patterns
  - state mutation
  - threat modelling
